        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most buyers the <strong class="text-white">Commercial 1750</strong> is the NordicTrack
            to buy: lifetime motor cover, decline as well as incline, and a pivoting screen, bought
            on discount. Walkers on a budget should look at the
            <strong class="text-white">T Series 10</strong>, and fast runners at the
            <strong class="text-white">Commercial 2450</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If steep incline is the goal, the <strong class="text-white">X16</strong> does everything
            the X24 does for less. Whichever you choose, check the specification for the current
            model year and budget for iFIT as an ongoing cost.
          </p>
